format session-log-v1
stamp 20260827.171055
editor Claude Code
model claude-fable-5
voice Kyri
host macOS clone (Mac hand) -- Eastern (EDT) one-clock
title a log is born on its day's shelf -- the fund takes its living name, and the room stops growing flat
prompt Keaton, mid-turn: molt anything still naming the old Seva fund (now Siya Fund LLC) and the two domains -- siya-ww.com rather than siya.fund, grain-ww.com rather than grainos.org -- and shed the fossils; and make every hand write its session log to date/YYYYMMDD/ by default, folding the unsorted flat logs and shedding what that molt leaves.
think The fund molt discriminated three senses of one word before touching anything: Seva is the VIEWER module and the Sanskrit word for selfless service, and only the FUND sense was his to rename. The fund was already Siya; what moved was the entity name to Siya Fund LLC and the two domains, seated in construction/domain-registry.bron with the elders kept as named anchors rather than deleted. The seed scrub learned all four spellings -- Siya Fund LLC, siya-ww.com, siya.fund, grain-ww.com, grainos.org -- because the press room SHIPS and a domain the scrub does not know is a domain the seed can carry.
think The founding announcement molted and its elder shed, and the one thing I refused is worth naming: the release argues PBC throughout -- the headline, the W.S. Title 17 Chapter 31 citation, the benefit-statement and annual-reporting promises -- and an LLC is a different form. The name and domain are carried because they were given; the legal framing is left standing under an ENTITY FORM gate for the Wyoming attorney the draft already said must read it. An agent renaming an entity type is an agent inventing a legal fact.
think The session-log law is the larger change and it is subtraction: a log is BORN at session-logs/date/YYYYMMDD/ with its row prepended to that day's shelf, so nothing folds afterward because nothing arrives loose. The guards allowed this by their own named rules -- log_has_a_row watches the flat room only, index_row_bound gates living pins while shelved rows keep every byte, and index_fold reads a stale row as one whose day has folded, which a born-folded room has none of. The living pin became what counsel's already is: the way in, one row per day, newest first, and it can no longer grow with the room. 139 closed-day logs folded by the tool, today's 22 by hand onto an OPEN shelf that freezes when the day closes.
obs The fold was blocked by a macOS gap in the tools' own resolver: tools/rye/enrich/root.rye reads /proc/self/cwd, which no BSD publishes. Two portable second readings were measured and BOTH refused -- Io.Dir.realPath resolves through /proc/self/fd in this std, and std.c.getcwd is the libc seam that would need an explicit -lc on the Linux pier that no caller passes, which is REDS %286's shape exactly. So the resolver now refuses by name, RootNeedsEnvOnThisHost, and points at its own documented environment door rather than surfacing a bare FileNotFound; the fold ran through that door.
obs Proven after: index_fold, log_has_a_row, index_row_bound, room_bound, dated_path, rule_twin, loop_prompt_parse, sow, living_docs_lint and tracked_link all GREEN; all six launchers print; the pin fell 7,293 to 6,904 bytes holding 36 shelf rows where it held 22 laps.
loom logs_folded=139 logs_born_folded=22 shelves=37 pin_bytes=6904 flat_logs=0 domains_seated=2 press_molted=1
file .claude/rules/session-logs.md the born-on-shelf law, and its Cursor twin beside it
file recursion-prompts/versions/20260826-180017_chatgpt-mind-macos-loop.md the ChatGPT hand learns the same shelf
file session-logs/README.md the pin becomes the way in -- one row per day
file construction/domain-registry.bron siya-ww.com and grain-ww.com seated, elders kept as anchors
file press/20260827-165527_siya-fund-llc-founding-announcement.md the mutant, with the entity-form gate named
file tools/rye/enrich/root.rye the refusal names its own door on a host without /proc
recommend keep-going -- the writings sweep across foundations and context is the last of the three; its fossils prep and shed on the same circled word
